    mission: { situation: 'You are Maya. Your tutor is Jisoo. Read the new campaign focus note. Explain the content choice and how you would answer Kai’s concern.', task: 'Present the combined approach, give a reason for testing it, and keep the artist’s identity in view.', roles: ['Jisoo', 'Maya'], title: 'Campaign focus note', text: '<p><strong>Campaign focus: introduce the music</strong></p><p>Use a series of short performances to introduce Kai’s sound. Keep useful footage so the team can also build a longer video. This combines the short-content idea with Luis’s interest in memorable visuals.</p><p>Test different performances before committing to a larger campaign. The budget remains limited; the note does not add funding or a fixed release date.</p><p>When Kai asks about becoming an online personality, explain that the aim is discovery. The content should help people hear his music without asking him to pretend to be a different person.</p><p>Review what works before choosing the next campaign step.</p>', lines: ['Maya, how does this plan combine our ideas?', 'Why keep the performance footage?', 'What is the benefit of testing before committing more resources?', 'Has the budget or release date changed in this note?', 'How would you answer Kai’s concern about his identity?', 'What should we review before the next step?'], evidence: 'Fresh note supplies the combined plan, testing reason and artist focus. No exact budget, fixed release date, paid advertising result or guaranteed platform success is given. These are the fictional team’s proposals, not current recommendations about real social platforms. Keep the nearly finished single distinct from published promotional material.', useful: ['The plan combines ... with ...', 'We need to work within ...', 'Testing would help us ...', 'The aim is to ...', 'We can promote ... without ...'] },
    topics: [['COMBINING IDEAS', ['How can you identify what two proposals have in common?', 'What makes a compromise useful rather than vague?', 'How can you explain why a plan fits the resources?']], ['PROMOTION', ['What should a first introduction tell an audience?', 'How can you test an idea on a modest scale?', 'Why separate a plan from a guaranteed result?']], ['IDENTITY', ['How can a public message reflect the person behind it?', 'What would you ask an artist before planning content?', 'Why can attention and authenticity both matter?']]],
